<!-- Like this title: a filled thumbs-up.

     The ACTIVE state of the detail header's like toggle (see
     ic_detail_thumb_up_outline, and ic_detail_bookmark_filled for the row's
     geometry): 24x24 viewport, the same box and baked kb_text_hi (#FFF3EFE4) as
     every other glyph in the row, so the button does not change size or weight
     when the signal lands. One mark that fills, rather than two unrelated
     glyphs.

     Path data is Google's Material Icons "thumb_up" (24 unit viewport), copied
     rather than hand-drawn: the forearm fills x 7..20 and the separate cuff bar
     sits at x 1..5, both solid, which is what makes the filled state read as a
     decision at the 18dp the header renders it at. -->
